From e5a64387192ddb92f91f1a021488dc36efad451e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Dagunts <ddagunts@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 23:02:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Port the kernel module to Linux 6.12 (ARM, MT5398)

- headers: asm/system.h gone, stddef.h/stdarg.h from linux/
- mm: __vmalloc() lost its pgprot: uncached/WC areas are pages + vmap()
  (VM_MAP_PUT_PAGES), flushed first; vmap() takes VM_MAP
- mmap: vm_flags_set(), vmf_insert_mixed()
- osfunc: timer_setup(), access_ok() without type, get_user_pages() and
  follow_pfnmap_start() for user page lookup, mmap_read_lock(), put_page();
  ARM cache range ops through __cpuc_flush_dcache_area + outer_cache (the
  dmac_* range functions are private to arch/arm/mm now)
- module: platform driver bound from the device tree (img,powervr-sgx544),
  void remove(), class_create(name), no MODULE_SUPPORTED_DEVICE, no
  suspend/resume
- proc: /proc/pvr not built (the 3.x procfs API is gone; nothing needs it)
- devicemem: TI's OMAP GEM unmap path only with SUPPORT_DRI_DRM_EXTERNAL

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
